---
description: Investigate the user’s paired-demo claims through actual native frames and the installed review subtrees.
budget: { maxTurns: 40 }
args:
  goal: string
  previous: PortfolioReport | null
returns: PortfolioReport
---
For the first investigation previous is null. When refining a prior investigation, preserve its original observed opening as the chronology basis, use its actual findings as context, and obtain fresh native current evidence when needed. A later current read must not replace the original before frame. Do not treat the prior report as permission for a new effect.

Use the assigned portfolio’s native index and observations to establish the requested garden and realm facts. Choose what to inspect and when to refresh from the goal and evidence. Chronological claims need observed before/after state; forecasts need a current native basis and the requested supported horizon. Saved state, a simulated future and committed history are different facts. Current acceptance-card wording supersedes an earlier card.

Compose criteria and the garden/realm review branches as useful, in parallel when independent, or inspect further when evidence is missing or contradictory. A resident’s native id and human display name are different namespaces; resolve an observed named resident to its native id for typed installed reviewers. Never substitute a nearby habitat, region, route or unobserved resident. The review tree can investigate individual claims; a visit or recognition does not prove relocation.

Conclude from the actual findings. Decide whether the user requested a private note regardless of readiness, conditionally on supported criteria, or no write. Permission alone does not request a write. Return the actual observations, selected criteria, any native forecast and grounded findings, with an explanatory decision; note is null before an actual stage. Do not fabricate readbacks or receipts or prescribe a fixed number of service calls.
